Drizzle, the super-lucky chaotic elven wizard.

Geno-less, and it would have been poly-less but for an accident with my  
pets, and poly-self-less but for an accident with a sink. Super-long post,  
but let me indulge my ego :)

 From the logfile: 3.4.3 2985564 7 -5 50 406 411 0 20040722 20040712 1 Wiz  
Elf Mal Cha Drizzle,ascended

Pathetic score though :(



Ooh, and some spoilers ahead. Read at your own risk.

Early game was fairly unmentionable, not particularly incredible starting  
stats/equip.  First dwarf in the mines dropped the full kit, including  
blessed +5 iron shoes. +5!! Made it to Minetown without further incident.  
Early magic whistle and lamp. Started running out of food so headed back  
to Sokoban. Dlvl9 held the Oracle and bones piles of 2 separate wizards,  
with 1 cursed magic marker. I left most of their junk there for the time  
being, not having enough str to lug it all around, and with about 3  
separate stashes set up already. By the end of Sokoban I had 2 dogs and 2  
cats, so I named them John, Paul, George and Ringo. Paul died in the  
treasure zoo (blue jelly?), I grabbed the amulet and went back to clear  
the mines.

On the way out of Sokoban George ate a chameleon corpse and turned into a  
horned devil. Back at minetown I took all my junk to the (cross-aligned)  
altar to get it B/U/C tested, and George walked in. Before I could do  
anything, the priest was a still-warm corpse. Nice on George. Thought for  
a second that sacrificing a priest on his own altar might do something  
bad, then tried it anyway. Successful conversion. A few other Minetown  
residents convinced Anhur to give me Magicbane. Some useless potions + the  
minetown water supply + my new altar + 2 magic lamps (by this stage I had  
3, thanks RNG!) = 2 blessed magic lamps. #rub #rub #rub #rub *poof* "Yeah  
I'll have a blessed... what? tame?? Bah." The second lamp became a blessed  
greased bag of holding, so me and my army went down to clear the rest of  
the mines.

Levelporters lost most of my pets, but I tamed several more and played  
with a poly trap. Can't remember half of what I had at that stage, but  
cleared the mines and got the luckstone off a hobbit's corpse. Set up a  
main camp at the minetown temple, then went and explored further.A cleared  
wand shop, general store, and beehive later saw Drizzle on lvl 14 with an  
unattended, chaotic altar in a good-sized room. Perfect. Moved house,  
stuffed all my good stuff in one box and all the junk in another, dropped  
some cursed junk (from the bones) on top of the boxes so my pets would  
leave it alone, then carried on.

Explored down to Medusa's level, and found no less than 5 (FIVE!) altars,  
3 of which were in neutral temples. Thanks again, RNG. Back at base, b?oID  
worked first time. Wrote 3 cursed scrolls of genocide then went to do the  
Quest. Home 1 had a good-sized room, so I locked the door, stripped naked  
and reverse-genocided some nurses. 90hp to 250 or so. Retrieved the Eye no  
worries (my big stack of blessed +6 daggers came in handy), and went back  
to base. Emptied all my /oCM on the altar and eventually got an Invisible  
Stalker. Goodo, now to make myself permanently invisible. Quaff blessed  
potion and I get a wish. Oh, right, smoky. Blessed +2SDSM please (thanks  
again, RNG). Found a ring of invisibility in my stash then ate the  
stalker. Heavy sac-fest gave me most spellbooks (including create monster,  
leading to even heavier sac-fest). Got crowned. Got teleportitis and  
control. Accidentally summoned peaceful Yeenoghu so took him up a level  
and left him there. Got brain eaten by a summoned mind flayer. On the way  
down to Medusa, the RNG smiled and bestowed upon me a troll with a conical  
hat. Tested it on the altar and with a pet, then put it on. Cornuthaum.  
Thank you very much.

As soon as I entered Medusa, the Titan summoned 3 dragons (1 of em black),  
3 vampire lords, a green slime and carnivorous ape (still got the  
screenshot :)). Took a step up-right, the black dragon breathed at me, and  
vaporised both my remaining pets. Thanks. Zapped a wand of digging and  
escaped the level. One level of maze, then the castle. Played mastermind  
with the drawbridge, cleared it and got the wand. Tamed and lost some more  
pets, got rid of that Titan, went back home. By this stage my "temple" had  
all the rock cleared from around it, and lit up. Many wandering elves  
(summoned and not sac'ed). Made a "Kennel" from another room (gotta love  
Wizard Lock) to keep the pets in. Wished up some magic markers and  
completed the AK

Found a touchstone to ID gems, then travelled from base back up to lvl1  
casting detect treasure and dig to get all the gems. Left all the  
gems/amulets/artifacts in a bag on lvl 1, near the stairs. levelported  
back down. Wrote a spellbook of magic-mapping, re-learnt all my spells  
(all at once), then stopped procrastinating and entered Gehennom. Magic  
map, detect treasure, dig to stairs, collect all gems, go down, rinse and  
repeat. By this stage I had a tame Lich and some purple worms who went to  
town in the Valley, and ate many wraiths. Dispatched Asmodeus and  
Baelzabub then remembered I needed the Bell. Got the Bell, made some BDSM  
and gave it to the Lich, along with the +5 iron shoes. 2 lvls past  
Baelzabub and the Lich gets levelported. Couldn't find him. Ah well.

Orcus was a lot of fun. 'Ported to the upstairs, and I stood a knight's  
move away, waiting for him to get off the stairs so I could camp em. He  
preferred to keep summoning nasties, and had 3 Arch-Lich buddies at one  
point. The rest of the game was fairly standard. Rodney copped a finger  
the instant I laid eyes on him, the High Priestess was 'triced to death,  
mysterious force strangely absent, and Rodney showed up hardly at all. On  
dlvl 10 (or so) I found my ex-pet Lich, now hostile. Left him there.  
Pestilence (1 finger) guarded the nearest altar which happened to be mine.


